# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Secrets — real flags/codes and env. NEVER commit these.
# (Kept explicit so they stay ignored even after the /deploy/ rule below
#  is removed post-event.)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
deploy/.env
deploy/secrets/
*.local.json

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# park-systems MCP server + organizer docs — organizer-only. Ignored FOR
# NOW so the pre-event commit is challenges-only and the flag values /
# unlock logic aren't exposed ahead of the CTF. Publish the server after
# the event by deleting this block (or `git add -f <path>`).
#
# Leading "/" anchors each rule to the repo root, so the challenges' own
# challenges/ctf04-capstone/cmd/ and .../internal/ dirs are NOT affected.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/cmd/
/internal/
/deploy/
/fixtures/
/docs/
/go.mod
/go.sum
/Dockerfile

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Compiled Go binaries (a main package builds to a file named after its dir).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/park-systems
/challenges/ctf01-welcome/ctf01-welcome
/challenges/ctf02-durable/ctf02-durable
/challenges/ctf03-mcp/ctf03-mcp
/challenges/ctf04-capstone/cmd/raptor-keeper/raptor-keeper
/challenges/ctf04-capstone/cmd/grid-ranger/grid-ranger
/challenges/ctf04-capstone/cmd/park-director/park-director
*.exe
*.test
*.out

# build dirs
/out/
/dist/
/vendor/
